<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">companion-stay</ansi>

Sets how far your companion may roam, and says where things stand if you
give it no argument. Telling them in your own words works too; this is the
plain switch, and it needs no conversation.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Usage ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">companion-stay</ansi>          What they are doing now.
  <ansi fg="command">companion-stay close</ansi>    At your side. They go nowhere unless you ask.
  <ansi fg="command">companion-stay normal</ansi>   With you, but they run errands when you ask.
  <ansi fg="command">companion-stay free</ansi>     Their own business, when nothing needs them.

Normal is the default. Whichever you choose, they still follow you from room
to room, defend you, and come back on their own if you get separated.
